{"name":"Belgian Block","hex":"#9ba29e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"block","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substantial, often approximately cuboid, piece of any substance.","A chopping block: a cuboid base for cutting or beheading."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fill or obstruct (something) so that it is not possible to pass.","To prevent (something or someone) from passing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/block"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sett (paving)","blocks":[{"text":"A sett, also known as a block or Belgian block, is a broadly rectangular quarried stone used in paving roads and walkways. Formerly in widespread use, particularly on steeper streets because setts provided horses' hooves with better grip than a smooth surface, they are now encountered more usually as decorative stone paving in landscape architecture. Setts may be referred to incorrectly as cobblestones, but a sett is distinct from a cobblestone in that it is quarried or worked to a regular shape, whereas the latter is generally a small, naturally rounded rock. Setts are usually made of granite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Camino_f%C3%A1cil.jpg/330px-Camino_f%C3%A1cil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sett_(paving)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Gatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg/500px-Gatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Gatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg/1280px-Gatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Gatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg/500px-Gatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Setts in pallet collars.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGatsten_i_pallkragar_-_Ystad-2021.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Eden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg/500px-Eden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Eden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg/1280px-Eden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Eden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg/500px-Eden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The setts at the junction of Eden Street and Criffel Street in Silloth-on-Solway, Cumbria, UK.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEden_Street_Silloth_on_Solway.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg/500px-2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg/1280px-2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg/500px-2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sett paving in Georgetown, Washington, D.C.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2019-09-16_16_23_25_Old_trolley_tracks_embedded_within_Belgian_block_pavement_along_P_Street_Northwest_in_Georgetown%2C_Washington%2C_D.C..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Circles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg/500px-Circles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Circles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg/1280px-Circles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Circles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg/500px-Circles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Samples of setts in Lysekil, Sweden, quarried and cut in Bohuslän, once a major producer of granite setts. The image has notations about the different types of setts; they can also be identified by an information board (in Swedish).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACircles_of_granite_sett_paving_next_to_Kungstorget_in_Lysekil_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/High_Street_setts%2C_Edinburgh.JPG/250px-High_Street_setts%2C_Edinburgh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/High_Street_setts%2C_